Package: dcorMix
Type: Package
Title: Pairwise Distance Correlation for Mixed-Type Variables
Version: 1.3.0
Date: 2026-08-23
Authors@R: person(given = "Surface",
              family = "User",
              role = c("aut", "cre"),
              email = "user@example.com")
Description: Computes pairwise distance correlation coefficients with
    permutation or asymptotic tests for variables of mixed types, including
    continuous, binary/ternary nominal, and binary/ternary ordinal variables.
    Applies type-specific encoding strategies (one-hot for nominal, integer
    encoding for ordinal, raw values for continuous) to ensure meaningful
    distance metrics. Missing values are handled via pairwise deletion, with
    per-pair sample sizes reported. Supports multiple-comparison correction
    (FDR, Bonferroni, etc.), partial distance correlation controlling for
    confounders, matrix-format conversion for 'corrplot', and a ggplot2-based
    heatmap (optionally clustered) for visualizing the distance correlation
    matrix. Built on the 'energy' package methodology by Szekely and Rizzo.
